From: Michael Narine <michael@verita-ai.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] example: no-op patch documenting the header format

This patch changes nothing. It exists so the patch tooling (apply_patches.py,
lint_patch_headers.py) and CI have a series to run on before the first real
patch (0001) lands in M2. It is skipped when applying and is not listed in
NOTICE. Delete it when the first real patch is added, or keep it as the
format reference.

Every real patch starts with this header, then a git-format-patch style
diff relative to the root of the Orca tree (no engine/ or third_party/
prefix). One purpose per patch (02 section 2); the one-line Purpose and the
Date are what the generated NOTICE lists (compliance.md 5a).

Purpose: Document the patch header format; no change to Orca.
